# Platform Auth Python Client

Private Python SDK for the central Platform Auth authorization service. Consumers
install the exact version and SHA-256 approved by Platform Auth's machine-readable
consumer contract manifest; human-maintained documentation does not define the
approved release.

The SDK serializes versioned requests, calls Platform Auth, and parses central
decisions. It never evaluates membership, roles, plans, subscriptions,
entitlements, or quotas locally and has no database access.

## Install

Consumers must install an exact version from the approved private registry:

```text
platform-auth-client==<approved-version>
```

The dependency-free core contains the standard-library synchronous client.
Optional extras are `aws-client`, `http-client`, and `fastapi`. See
[Private installation](docs/installation.md) for CodeArtifact authentication and
CI guidance. The approval source is
`platform-auth-service/tests/fixtures/consumer-authorization-contract/manifest.json`.

## Use

```python
from platform_auth_client import RemoteAuthorizationClient
from platform_auth_client.client import SigV4HttpTransport
from platform_auth_client.config import RemoteClientConfig

config = RemoteClientConfig.from_env()
transport = SigV4HttpTransport(config, region="us-east-1")
auth = RemoteAuthorizationClient(transport)
```

The calling service supplies approved workload credentials. Delegated user
access tokens are forwarded only as opaque decision inputs and must never be
logged. See [Usage and compatibility](docs/usage.md) for decision, FastAPI,
Cognito M2M, async, retry, and contract-version guidance.

